meta {
  name: 05_AuthorizationBoundaries
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  Scenario: Only the parties of a consent request can read and answer it

    Given the enterprise has created a consent request for the person
    When another enterprise reads the request, the request is forbidden
    When the enterprise reads an unknown request id, the request is not found
    When another person reads the request in the portal, the request is forbidden
    When another person counts the person's requests, the request is unauthorized
    When another person lists the person's requests, the request is unauthorized
    When another person accepts the request, the request is forbidden
    When another person rejects the request, the request is forbidden
    When another person reads the consent, the request is forbidden
    When the person accepts without a language, the request fails validation
    When the person counts with an unknown status, the request fails validation
    When the person revokes a request that was never accepted, the request fails
    And the request is rejected by the person to close it

  The last step answers the request so it does not stay pending in the person's portal.
}
